  "edits": "head: 'other' puts other_head in place of the checkpoint head; 'set:X' puts the string X; 'upper' puts the head in capitals; 'newline' adds a line end after it. digest: 'other' sets the anchor's digest field to other_head; 'absent' removes the field. response is one edit or a list of edits applied in order to the decoded response: 'truncate:N' keeps the first N bytes; 'append:HH' adds the bytes HH (hex) after it; 'patch:P:HH' writes HH over the bytes at position P; 'splice:P:N:HH' takes N bytes out at position P and puts HH there; 'set:X' puts the string X in place of the base64 text; 'absent' removes the field. 'was' is what stands at the first edit's position before it (hex): a harness stops if it does not, so that an edit cannot land on the wrong field. token (anchor_vectors, given to the function that reads one anchor): 'absent' removes token_blob; 'value:J' puts the JSON value J in its place; 'cut:N' keeps its first N characters; 'wrap_in_list' puts it inside a one-element list; 'nest:N' puts an object whose one value is a list nested until the text holds N opening brackets; 'digits:N' puts an object whose one value is a number of N digits.",
