  "wiring_note": "The wiring cases are written out in each harness under exactly these names; a harness fails if the names it ran are not this list. Six of them edit the bundle as served (or read the planted one) and check that the result reaches the verdict and the lines; one of those holds the three verifiers to one reading of an anchors field that is not a list (it is not read). The other nine use a fixture made with test keys. A timestamp that does not bind, on a checkpoint that no entry cites, must fail the bundle through the checkpoint's own line. A head that is not its last entry's hash must be rejected; a bundle without the last entry must say that nothing ties the head to an entry; a heartbeat checkpoint (no new entry, the head of the one before it) must pass. Then the end of a checkpoint, which nobody signs: an entry outside the stated range, an end moved to an earlier entry, and an end moved past the last entry must each be rejected, because only the last leaf of the tree has a proof with no sibling on the right. The entry a checkpoint ends at counts only when its own proof puts it last under the checkpoint's root: an entry can be restated at another seq by anyone, so one found by its seq alone proves nothing. Last, a checkpoint with a malformed id must be rejected even when a valid one with the same text form follows it."
